<!--
  Agent mark.

  Drawn on a 2048 viewport because the source artwork is drawn at that size.
  Android scales the drawable to the size asked of it, so this only sets the
  default; every call site sets its own size.

  The <group> is the whole reason the mark looked undersized. The artwork
  occupies x 548..1492 and y 403..1648 of a 2048 square — 46% of the width
  and 61% of the height — so at a 24dp call site the visible mark was 11 x
  14.6dp while the lucide glyphs beside it filled their 22dp box. The mark was
  drawn at half the size of its neighbours and no amount of iconSize fiddling
  fixes that, because the empty viewport, not the size, was the problem.

  The group scales the artwork to fill the box with a 6% margin and re-centres
  it, so it now matches the optical weight of the icons next to it. The centre
  is the centre of the artwork's own bounds including the eyes, not of the
  viewport, which is why the two translate values differ.

  The eyes are cut as holes with evenOdd rather than painted in a second
  colour. Compose's Icon() applies its own ColorFilter over the whole drawable,
  so a two-tone path collapses to one flat colour the moment it is tinted and
  the eyes vanish into the body. A hole cannot be filled by a tint.
-->
